   "evidence": "OrderExtension.lean:47 `def extensionCone (f : K \u2192+* L) : Subsemiring L where __ := AddSubmonoid.closure (weightedSquares f)`; public API at lines 61-100 is `subset`, `induction`, `mul_self_mem`, `map_mem_of_nonneg`, `map_nonneg`, `nonneg` only (grep `extensionCone\\.` shows no `le_iff`/`toAddSubmonoid`); Extension.lean:70-79 provides `adjoin_le`/`adjoin_le_iff` for the analogous generated preordering.",
   "file": "TauCeti/FieldTheory/RealClosure/OrderExtension.lean",
   "fix": "Add `theorem extensionCone_toAddSubmonoid (f) : (extensionCone f).toAddSubmonoid = AddSubmonoid.closure (weightedSquares f) := rfl` and `@[simp] theorem extensionCone_le_iff {S : Subsemiring L} : extensionCone f \u2264 S \u2194 weightedSquares f \u2286 S` (mp from `extensionCone.subset`, mpr via `AddSubmonoid.closure_le`), mirroring `adjoin_le_iff`; optionally derive `extensionCone.nonneg` from it.",
   "issue": "`extensionCone f` is the subsemiring generated by `weightedSquares f` with a hidden body, but its only elimination form is `extensionCone.induction`; there is no universal property `extensionCone f \u2264 S \u2194 weightedSquares f \u2286 S` and no `*_def`-style restatement `(extensionCone f).toAddSubmonoid = AddSubmonoid.closure (weightedSquares f)`, so consumers cannot use Mathlib's `closure_le`/`closure_induction` API without reproving it, and `extensionCone.nonneg` (line 94) is an ad hoc instance of the missing lemma.",
   "line": 47
  }
 ],
